    {
      "text": "tree of the knowledge … thou shalt not eat, Gen. 2:17 (Moses 3:17). in the day ye eat thereof, then your eyes shall be opened, Gen. 3:5 (Moses 4:11). blood thereof, shall ye not eat, Gen. 9:4. Egyptians … not eat bread with the Hebrews, Gen. 43:32. passover: There shall no stranger eat thereof, Ex. 12:43. Ye shall not eat any thing with the blood, Lev. 19:26. land that eateth up the inhabitants thereof, Num. 13:32. These are the beasts which ye shall eat, Deut. 14:4. touched him, and said unto him, Arise and eat, 1 Kgs. 19:5. zeal of thine house hath eaten me up, Ps. 69:9 (John 2:17). thou shalt eat the labour of thine hands, Ps. 128:2. they eat of the fruit of their own way, Prov. 1:31. they shall eat the fruit of their doings, Isa. 3:10 (2 Ne. 13:10). We will eat our own bread, Isa. 4:1 (2 Ne. 14:1). Butter and honey shall he eat, Isa. 7:15 (2 Ne. 17:15). lion shall eat straw like the ox, Isa. 11:7 (65:25). eat and drink; for to morrow, Isa. 22:13 (1 Cor. 15:32; 2 Ne. 28:7). moth shall eat them up like a garment, Isa. 51:8. he that hath no money; come ye, buy, and eat, Isa. 55:1. my servants shall eat, but ye shall be hungry, Isa. 65:13. shall eat up thine harvest, and thy bread, Jer. 5:17. Thy words were found, and I did eat them, Jer. 15:16. cause them to eat the flesh of their sons, Jer. 19:9. fathers have eaten a sour grape, Jer. 31:29 (Ezek. 18:2). Son of man, eat that thou findest; eat this roll, Ezek. 3:1. Nebuchadnezzar … did eat grass as oxen, Dan. 4:33. For they shall eat, and not have enough, Hosea 4:10 (Hag. 1:6). Thou shalt eat, but not be satisfied, Micah 6:14.",
